<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mehmed IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1642">1642</a>–<a href="/years/1693">1693</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Mehmed the Hunter</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mehmed IV was Ottoman sultan from 1648 to 1687, coming to the throne aged six. Real power passed to the Köprülü grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">viziers</a>, who restored order and won <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/podolia">Podolia</a>. His reign ended in disaster after the failed siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1683 and the losses that followed, and he was deposed in 1687. He was known for his passion for hunting.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mehmed-iv.jpg" alt="Mehmed IV" width="320" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Koppmayer, Jacob (1640-1701) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahomet_IV._sonst_Achmet_genannt_T%C3%BCrckischer_Ka%C3%BFser.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
